@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- Israel: what else in the Interpretation Law 5741-1981 and the Interpretation Ordinance [New Version] is
-- computable, on top of the time rules in il-interpretation-time.l4.
--
-- Sources (unofficial Wikisource consolidations; the official texts could not be fetched):
--   the Law, ../../source/law.wiki, cited as src:N; the Ordinance, ../../source/ordinance.wiki, cited as src:ordinance:N.
-- Everything here takes its facts as inputs. Sections that are canons of construction with nothing to compute
-- are carried as quoted text in il-interpretation-carried-text.l4 and listed in NOTES.md.

§ `Interpretation Law 5741-1981 and Interpretation Ordinance: the other computable provisions`

§§ `Nouns`

-- Law s 1 and s 2 both end "if there is no other provision on the matter and nothing in the matter or its
-- context is inconsistent with" the Law (s 2: "that definition"). Those two facts are judgements the caller makes.
DECLARE `The matter in question` HAS
    `another provision deals with it`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- The words of Law s 3 that this module's rules depend on.
DECLARE `A word the Law defines` IS ONE OF
    `the word day`
    `the word month`
    `the word year`
    `the word fiscal year`
    `the word מימי חופין`
    `the word חטא`
    `the word עוון`
    `the word פשע`

DECLARE `Source of a definition` IS ONE OF
    `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
    `the definition in section 1 of the Interpretation Ordinance`

DECLARE `Binding text of an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `the text in the language in which the enactment was given`
    `the new text fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance`

DECLARE `The text of an enactment` HAS
    `given in English before the State was established`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a new text was fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance`  IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment` HAS
    `slight`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `harms the essential`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `misleads`                              IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What becomes of regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment` IS ONE OF
    `they lapse with the repealed enactment`
    `they stand until they are cancelled by regulations and appointments under the repealing enactment`

DECLARE `An enactment's effect on the State` HAS
    `it would derogate from a right of the State or impose a duty on it`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it says so expressly`                                                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A regulation measured against s 16(4) of the Ordinance` HAS
    `the power to make it was conferred by a law`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `it contradicts a provision of a law`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `another intention is implied`                     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement` HAS
    `the day the enactment was given`                                                  IS A DATE
    `the day the enactment commences`                                                  IS A DATE
    `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `another intention is implied`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `The earliest day s 19 of the Ordinance lets a regulation be valid` IS ONE OF
    `not before the day the enactment commences` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `s 19 sets no earliest day`

§§ `Named refusals`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`a day-level date cannot say whether an enactment given on the day the Law commenced was given before 00:01 on that day` MEANS
    REFUSE "a day-level date cannot say whether an enactment given on the day the Law commenced was given before 00:01 on that day"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Ordinance text defines no day: the Law's s 3 does not reach a word in an enactment given before the Law, and the Ordinance has no entry for it` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Ordinance text defines no day: the Law's s 3 does not reach a word in an enactment given before the Law, and the Ordinance has no entry for it"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that"

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 31 saves subsections (2) and (4) of section 16 of the Ordinance but not the section as a whole, so a question about the whole section has no single answer` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 31 saves subsections (2) and (4) of section 16 of the Ordinance but not the section as a whole, so a question about the whole section has no single answer"

§§ `Law s 32 — when the Law commenced, and s 21 applied to it`

-- src:162 | תחילתו של חוק זה ביום ג׳ בתשרי התשמ״ב (1 באוקטובר 1981).
@ref Interpretation Law s 32 (src:162)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced` MEANS
    YMD 1981 10 1

@ref Interpretation Law s 32 (src:162); s 21 (quoted in il-interpretation-time.l4)
GIVETH A Moment
`s 32, s 21 — the moment the Interpretation Law began to bind` MEANS
    `s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` `s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced`

§§ `Law s 1 — the Law governs unless another provision or the context says otherwise`

-- src:22 | חוק זה יחול לגבי כל חיקוק והוראת מינהל, אף אם ניתנו לפני תחילתו, אם אין הוראה אחרת לענין הנדון ואם אין בענין הנדון או בהקשרו דבר שאינו מתיישב עם חוק זה; אולם על מלים וביטויים למעט ”חטא“, ”עוון“ ו”פשע“, שבחיקוקים והוראות מינהל שניתנו לפני תחילת חוק זה לא יחול
-- src:22 | סעיף 3 אלא יוסיפו לחול ההגדרות
-- src:22 | שבסעיף 1 לפקודת הפרשנות.
@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22)
GIVEN matter IS A `The matter in question`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — the Law governs` matter MEANS
        NOT matter's `another provision deals with it`
    AND NOT matter's `something in it or its context is inconsistent with the Law`

-- "Given before the commencement of this Law". An enactment is given at a moment, and the Law binds from 00:01 on
-- 1981-10-01 (s 32 with s 21). A day-level date settles every day except that one.
@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22); s 32 (src:162)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   d BELOW `s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced`
        THEN TRUE
        IF   d ABOVE `s 32 — the day the Interpretation Law commenced`
        THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE `a day-level date cannot say whether an enactment given on the day the Law commenced was given before 00:01 on that day`

@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22); s 21 (quoted in il-interpretation-time.l4); s 32 (src:162)
GIVEN m IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given at` m MEANS
    `the number of seconds up to` m LESS THAN `the number of seconds up to` `s 32, s 21 — the moment the Interpretation Law began to bind`

-- s 3 does not apply to the words of an enactment given before the Law, except חטא, עוון and פשע (the three
-- offence grades s 3 defines by reference to the Penal Law; named in s 1) and "fiscal year" (whose own
-- definition says, "notwithstanding s 1", that it applies to earlier enactments too). "Coastal waters"
-- (מימי חופין) is the fifth: the note under its definition in s 3 says that, by s 1(b) of the Coastal Waters Law
-- (a statute that is not among the sources), the definition applies to earlier enactments as well. That one
-- rests on the note and not on the Law's operative text.
-- src:47 | ”מימי חופין“ – רצועת ים פתוח לאורך חופי המדינה, ברוחב שנים עשר מילים ימיים מנקודת שפל המים שבחוף;
-- src:48 | לפי
-- src:48 | סעיף 1(ב) לחוק מימי חופין, תשי״ז–1956 ההגדרה ”מימי חופין“ חלה גם על חיקוקים שניתנו לפני תחילתו של חוק זה.
@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22); s 3 "fiscal year" (quoted in il-interpretation-time.l4); s 3 "coastal waters" and its note (src:47-48)
GIVEN w IS A `A word the Law defines`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 — section 3 applies to` w `in an enactment given on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `the word fiscal year` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the word מימי חופין`  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the word חטא`         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the word עוון`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the word פשע`         THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOT `s 1 — it was before the Law commenced that an enactment was given on` d

-- Which words the Ordinance text still defines for the earlier enactments: "year" and "month" (Gregorian).
-- It has no entry for "day". Its entries for "fiscal year", "coastal waters", חטא, עוון and פשע are marked
-- repealed ("(בוטלה)") and carry only a note saying what Law s 3 now provides.
-- src:ordinance:107 | ”שנה“ ו”חודש“ – למנין הלוח הגריגוריאני;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 1 "year" and "month" (src:ordinance:107)
GIVEN w IS A `A word the Law defines`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `the word month` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the word year`  THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Interpretation Law s 1 (src:22); Interpretation Ordinance s 1 (src:ordinance:107)
GIVEN w IS A `A word the Law defines`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Source of a definition`
`s 1 — the definition that governs` w `in an enactment given on` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `s 1 — section 3 applies to` w `in an enactment given on` d
        THEN `the definition in section 3 of the Interpretation Law`
        IF   `Ordinance s 1 — the Ordinance text still defines` w
        THEN `the definition in section 1 of the Interpretation Ordinance`
        OTHERWISE `the Ordinance text defines no day: the Law's s 3 does not reach a word in an enactment given before the Law, and the Ordinance has no entry for it`

-- "Year" and "month" in an enactment given before the Law are the Ordinance's: by the Gregorian calendar, with
-- no Hebrew-calendar clause. In a later enactment they are s 3's.
@ref Interpretation Law s 3 "year" and "month" (quoted in il-interpretation-time.l4); Interpretation Ordinance s 1 (src:ordinance:107)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      spec IS A `Specification of a period of years or months`
GIVETH A Calendar
`s 1, s 3, Ordinance s 1 — the calendar of a year or month in an enactment given on` d `, for a period specified as` spec MEANS
    IF   `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word year` `in an enactment given on` d
    THEN `s 3 — the calendar of a year or month specified as` spec
    ELSE `the Gregorian calendar`

§§ `Law s 20 — an act imposed on several persons`

-- src:119 | פעולה שהוטלה על מספר בני אדם כשרה אם נעשתה בידי רובם.
@ref Interpretation Law s 20 (src:119)
GIVEN total IS A NUMBER
      acted IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20 — an act imposed on` total `persons was validly done when` acted `of them did it` MEANS
    IF   total AT LEAST 1 AND acted AT LEAST 0 AND acted AT MOST total AND total EQUALS (TRUNC total 0) AND acted EQUALS (TRUNC acted 0)
    THEN (acted TIMES 2) GREATER THAN total
    ELSE `s 20 speaks of an act imposed on several persons and done by some of them; the numbers given do not fit that`

§§ `Law s 22(2) — a repeal cannot reach an earlier act`

-- src:127 | ביטולו של דין אין כוחו יפה –
-- src:128 | (1) להחיות דבר שלא היה לו תוקף בשעה שהביטול נכנס לתקפו;
-- src:129 | (2) להשפיע על פעולה קודמת של הדין המבוטל או על מה שנעשה לפיו;
-- src:130 | (3) להשפיע על זכות או חיוב שלפי הדין המבוטל.
-- Only limb (2) is computed. Limbs (1) and (3) are carried as text in il-interpretation-carried-text.l4.
@ref Interpretation Law s 22(2) (src:129); s 21 (quoted in il-interpretation-time.l4)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      act IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) — a repeal commencing on` d `is powerless to affect an act done at` act MEANS
    `the number of seconds up to` act LESS THAN `the number of seconds up to` (`s 21 — the moment a statute begins to bind, commencing on` d)

§§ `Law s 23 — regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment`

-- src:133 | משבוטל חיקוק, בטלים עמו התקנות והמינויים שנעשו מכוחו; אולם מקום שהחיקוק המבטל קובע הוראות במקום המבוטלות – התקנות והמינויים שנעשו מכוח ההוראות המבוטלות יעמדו בתקפם עד שיבוטלו בתקנות ובמינויים מכוח החיקוק המבטל.
@ref Interpretation Law s 23 (src:133)
GIVEN replaced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What becomes of regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment`
`s 23 — the regulations and appointments made under a repealed enactment, where the repealing enactment provides provisions in their place:` replaced MEANS
    IF   replaced
    THEN `they stand until they are cancelled by regulations and appointments under the repealing enactment`
    ELSE `they lapse with the repealed enactment`

§§ `Law s 24 — the binding text`

-- src:136 | הנוסח המחייב של כל דין הוא הנוסח שבשפה שבה הוא ניתן; אולם בדין שניתן באנגלית לפני הקמת המדינה ונקבע לו נוסח חדש לפי
-- src:136 | סעיף 16 לפקודת סדרי השלטון והמשפט, התש״ח–1948 – הנוסח החדש מחייב.
@ref Interpretation Law s 24 (src:136)
GIVEN text IS A `The text of an enactment`
GIVETH A `Binding text of an enactment`
`s 24 — the binding text of an enactment:` text MEANS
    IF   text's `given in English before the State was established` AND text's `a new text was fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance`
    THEN `the new text fixed under section 16 of the Law and Administration Ordinance`
    ELSE `the text in the language in which the enactment was given`

§§ `Law s 26 — deviation from a form`

-- src:142 | טופס שנקבע בחיקוק – סטיה קלה ממנו, שאין בה כדי לפגוע בעיקר או להטעות, אינה פוסלת את הנעשה לפיו.
@ref Interpretation Law s 26 (src:142)
GIVEN deviation IS A `A deviation from a form fixed in an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26 — the deviation disqualifies what was done under the form:` deviation MEANS
    NOT (        deviation's `slight`
             AND NOT deviation's `harms the essential`
             AND NOT deviation's `misleads`)

§§ `Law s 31 — what is left of the Ordinance`

-- src:159 | פקודת הפרשנות, למעט
-- src:159 | סעיפים 16(2) ו־(4),
-- src:159 | 17,
-- src:159 | 19
-- src:159 | ו־42 – בטלה.
@ref Interpretation Law s 31 (src:159)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      subsection IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 31 — the Ordinance's section` section `, subsection` subsection `, survives the Law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   section EQUALS 16
        THEN CONSIDER subsection
             WHEN JUST sub THEN (sub EQUALS 2) OR (sub EQUALS 4)
             WHEN NOTHING  THEN `s 31 saves subsections (2) and (4) of section 16 of the Ordinance but not the section as a whole, so a question about the whole section has no single answer`
        IF   section EQUALS 17 OR section EQUALS 19 OR section EQUALS 42
        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Law s 33 — publication`

-- src:165 | חוק זה יפורסם תוך שלושים ימים מיום קבלתו בכנסת.
@ref Interpretation Law s 33 (src:165); s 10(a) (quoted in il-interpretation-time.l4)
GIVEN adopted IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 33 — the last day for publishing a law adopted by the Knesset on` adopted MEANS
    `s 10(a) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` adopted

-- src:167 | נתקבל בכנסת ביום ט״ז באייר התשמ״א (20 במאי 1981).
@ref Interpretation Law, note of adoption after s 33 (src:167)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the Knesset adopted the Interpretation Law` MEANS
    YMD 1981 5 20

§§ `Interpretation Ordinance s 16(4) — a regulation may not contradict a law`

-- src:ordinance:165 | מקום שהחוק מעניק לרשות את הסמכות להתקין תקנות, יהיו ההוראות הבאות חלות לגבי התקנתן וכוח פעולתן של תקנות אלו, אם אין כוונה אחרת משתמעת –
-- src:ordinance:169 | (4) לא תהא תקנה סותרת הוראותיו של כל חוק;
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 16(4) (src:ordinance:165-169)
GIVEN regulation IS A `A regulation measured against s 16(4) of the Ordinance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 16(4) — s 16(4) forbids the regulation:` regulation MEANS
        regulation's `the power to make it was conferred by a law`
    AND regulation's `it contradicts a provision of a law`
    AND NOT regulation's `another intention is implied`

§§ `Interpretation Ordinance s 19 — using a power before the enactment commences`

-- src:ordinance:181 | חיקוק שאין תחילת תקפו עם נתינתו, והוא מעניק סמכות להתקין תקנות או לעשות מינוי או כל דבר למען מטרת החיקוק, אפשר להשתמש באותה סמכות – אם אין כוונה אחרת משתמעת – בכל שעה לאחר נתינתו של החיקוק, במידה שהדבר נראה דרוש או ראוי כדי להפעיל את החיקוק ביום תחילת תקפו; ואולם כל תקנה וכל מינוי וכל דבר שנעשו בכוח אותה סמכות לא יהיה להם תוקף עד יום תחילת תקפו של החיקוק, אלא אם היתה כוונה אחרת משתמעת מתוך החיקוק, או אם היו התקנה, המינוי או הדבר דרושים להפעלת החיקוק.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 19 (src:ordinance:181)
GIVEN power IS A `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement`
      x IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 19 — s 19 permits using the power of` power `on` x MEANS
        power's `the day the enactment commences` ABOVE power's `the day the enactment was given`
    AND x AT LEAST power's `the day the enactment was given`
    AND x BELOW power's `the day the enactment commences`
    AND power's `using the power seems necessary or proper to operate the enactment on its commencement day`
    AND NOT power's `another intention is implied`

-- What was done under the power has no validity "עד" (until) the day the enactment commences, unless another
-- intention is implied or what was done was needed to operate the enactment. READING TAKEN, see the fork register
-- in NOTES.md: "until" here is exclusive, so validity begins ON the commencement day. Read with Law s 8 it would
-- include that day, and nothing done under the power would be valid on the day the enactment first binds, which
-- defeats what the section is for; the context exception of Law s 1 is taken to switch s 8 off here.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 19 (src:ordinance:181)
GIVEN power IS A `A power that an enactment gives before its commencement`
      neededToOperate IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The earliest day s 19 of the Ordinance lets a regulation be valid`
`Ordinance s 19 — the earliest day a regulation made under the power of` power `may be valid, when it was needed to operate the enactment:` neededToOperate MEANS
    IF   neededToOperate OR power's `another intention is implied`
    THEN `s 19 sets no earliest day`
    ELSE `not before the day the enactment commences` (power's `the day the enactment commences`)

§§ `Interpretation Ordinance s 42 — the rights of the State`

-- src:ordinance:254 | אין חיקוק בא לגרוע מכל זכות של המדינה, או להטיל עליה חובה, אלא אם נאמר בו במפורש.
@ref Interpretation Ordinance s 42 (src:ordinance:254)
GIVEN effect IS AN `An enactment's effect on the State`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Ordinance s 42 — the enactment derogates from a right of the State or imposes a duty on it:` effect MEANS
        effect's `it would derogate from a right of the State or impose a duty on it`
    AND effect's `it says so expressly`
